failed only].\n\nCurrent state of the implementation (services/worker/src/rag_worker/report.py):\n- implements started/progress/done/failed exactly per the stub docstrings;\n  run_stage left as stub (red tests in tests/unit/test_run_stage.py belong to\n  T-worker-009, expected to stay red).\n- verify cmd 1 (ruff format --check + ruff check + mypy src) passes.\n- verify cmd 2 (pytest tests/unit/test_reporter.py): 4 passed, 3 failed \u2014 exactly the\n  3 tests above; the 3 failures fail on the contradictory full-list assertions, not on\n  callback content or ordering (e.g. api.calls[-2:] == [\"result\", \"stage.completed\"]\n  passes; FakeApi.started/results match expected dicts).\n\nSuggested fix for the planner: in the locked test, replace the full-list equality\nasserts on ctx[\"events\"].events (lines 132, 166, 191) with tail checks (e.g.\nevents[-1:] == [(RUN_ID, terminal_event)]) and change line 190 to\napi.calls[-3:] == [\"result\", \"stage.failed\"] (keeping the \"started\"/\"stage.started\"\nprefix from started()). Do not edit report.py to fix this \u2014 it is docstring-correct;\nany change there would break test 1 instead of fixing tests 5/6/7."
